From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:28:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: move the DSCP Policy state of a moved association

hostapd_ml_move_assoc_sta() gives the association of a non-AP MLD to
another link STA, and the caller then frees the old association STA.
ap_free_sta() frees its DSCP policies, so the non-AP MLD loses the
policies that the AP configured, and the dialog token and the state of
the DSCP Policy exchange start again.

Move the policies, the DSCP Policy state and the dialog token to the
new association STA.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include "scs.h"
 #include "accounting.h"
 #include "ieee802_1x.h"
+#include "robust_av.h"
 
 
 static u16 ieee80211_eht_ppet_size(u16 ppe_thres_hdr, const u8 *phy_cap_info)
@@ -1681,6 +1682,16 @@ struct sta_info * hostapd_ml_move_assoc_
 	accounting_sta_move(hapd, sta, *assoc_hapd, assoc_sta);
 	ieee802_1x_move_station(*assoc_hapd, sta, assoc_sta);
 #ifdef CONFIG_ROBUST_AV
+	free_dscp_policies(assoc_sta);
+	assoc_sta->policies = sta->policies;
+	assoc_sta->num_dscp_policies = sta->num_dscp_policies;
+	sta->policies = NULL;
+	sta->num_dscp_policies = 0;
+	assoc_sta->dscp_reset = sta->dscp_reset;
+	assoc_sta->unsolicited_dialog_token = sta->unsolicited_dialog_token;
+	assoc_sta->dscp_state = sta->dscp_state;
+#endif /* CONFIG_ROBUST_AV */
+#ifdef CONFIG_ROBUST_AV
 	os_memcpy(assoc_sta->scs_active, sta->scs_active,
 		  sizeof(sta->scs_active));
 	os_memset(sta->scs_active, 0, sizeof(sta->scs_active));
